# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# build output
/dist/
/outputs/
/work/

# scratch space for OCR runs, benchmark candidates and built helper binaries
/.tmp/

# Local fixture media. Deliberately not tracked: these are large (~1.3GB) and
# derived from commercial discs. Tests use the small synthetic fixtures in
# tests/fixtures instead; the full set only drives the local `ocr:gate` run.
#
# The `*` is not decoration: NTFS forbids `:` in a filename, so copying this
# corpus onto Windows renames it to U+F022 (the private-use character Windows
# substitutes). A literal `/sub:idx examples/` therefore matches nothing on
# Windows and one `git add -A` stages the whole corpus. `?` will not do here
# either — git matches byte-wise and U+F022 is three UTF-8 bytes.
/Subtitle Examples/
/sub*idx examples/

# Local working notes, not for publication
/RUNNING_NOTES.md
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/
